 answer='<strong>Three active copyright strikes terminate a YouTube channel.</strong> Each strike can be resolved if the claimant retracts it or if you file a valid counter notification and the claimant does not take legal action. Removing even one strike can be the basis for reinstatement. Termination appeals for Community Guidelines do not resolve copyright strikes.',
